# Caesar Salad

Based on [https://www.seriouseats.com/caesar-salad-recipe](https://www.seriouseats.com/caesar-salad-recipe) (wayback unavailable)

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Dressing

- [ ] 2 [garlic cloves]{ ing="garlic-cloves" }, minced
- [ ] 1 tsp [Dijon mustard]{ ing="dijon-mustard" }
- [ ] 2 tsp [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [Worcestershire sauce]{ ing="worcestershire-sauce" }
- [ ] 1/4 cup [mayonnaise]{ ing="mayonnaise" }
- [ ] 1/4 cup [grated Parmesan cheese]{ ing="grated-parmesan-cheese" }
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" }
- [ ] [Salt and black pepper]{ ing="salt-and-black-pepper" }, to taste

### Salad

- [ ] 2 heads [romaine lettuce]{ ing="romaine-lettuce" }, chopped into bite-sized pieces
- [ ] 1/2 cup [Parmesan cheese]{ ing="parmesan-cheese" }, shaved or grated
- [ ] 1.5 cups [croutons]{ ing="croutons" }
- [ ] (Optional) [Grilled chicken breast]{ ing="grilled-chicken-breast" }, sliced

## Recipe

1. Make the dressing: In a medium bowl, whisk together garlic, [Dijon mustard]{ ing="dijon-mustard" }, [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }, and [Worcestershire sauce]{ ing="worcestershire-sauce" }. Add [mayonnaise]{ ing="mayonnaise" } and Parmesan, whisk until smooth. Slowly drizzle in [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" } while whisking. Season with salt and [pepper]{ ing="salt-and-black-pepper" }
1. Prep the [lettuce]{ ing="romaine-lettuce" }: Wash and dry romaine thoroughly. Chop into bite-sized pieces
1. Assemble: In a large bowl, toss romaine with dressing until well coated. Add [croutons]{ ing="croutons" } and Parmesan, toss gently
1. Serve immediately

## Notes

1. For healthier version: Use Greek yogurt instead of mayonnaise, or reduce dressing amount
1. Make-ahead: Dressing can be refrigerated for up to 3 days
1. For croutons: Cube bread, toss with olive oil and garlic powder, bake at 375F for 10-15 minutes until golden
1. Add protein: Top with grilled chicken, salmon, or shrimp for a complete meal
